+The geometric residual evaluates the ideal implicit or conjugated tangent
+at numerical states. A separate finite-difference check of the implemented
+one-step output is recorded at a representative state with three
+differencing scales; neither check makes floating-point Newton iterations
+exactly structure preserving. The chart's known structure and preprocessing
+cost are disclosed. These examples establish a computable extension for
+specified models, while construction of a useful chart for a general
+high-dimensional catheter remains a separate computational problem.
